From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QED64 Toolchain <qed64-toolchain@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:42:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/20] cleanup: remove wasm32-era debug instrumentation; fix
 lean_shell_main arity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Remove the bring-up logging that accumulated during the wasm32 effort
across Shell.lean, Frontend.lean, Import.lean, initialize/init.cpp,
util/io.h and util/shell.cpp — the [DEBUG:*] prints plus a few adjacent
non-tagged bring-up logs — including an argv walker that indexed the JS
heap via HEAPU32 with a 4-byte stride (wrong under LP64) and two
pointer-to-int debug casts.

Also corrects util/shell.cpp's declaration and call of `lean_shell_main` to
the generated two-argument ABI (args, opts): the stale three-argument form
passed an extra `lean_box(0)` "world" token that the generated definition
does not take. Tolerated by past linkers; not a valid cross-TU C contract.

Upstreaming: the arity fix is relevant wherever this shell shim exists; the
debug removals are fork hygiene.
---
 src/Lean/Elab/Frontend.lean |   7 +-
 src/Lean/Elab/Import.lean   |   2 -
 src/Lean/Shell.lean         |   7 --
 src/initialize/init.cpp     |  61 ------------
 src/util/io.h               |  13 ---
 src/util/shell.cpp          | 186 +-----------------------------------
 6 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 273 deletions(-)

